---
# Source of the judge's-role diagram on /changelog (The swarm's judge entry).
# Baked in twice as inline SVG: this source (LR) above 760px, and below it
# judge-narrow.mmd, the same flow top to bottom, since a wide chain does not
# read at phone width. Render with Mermaid 11 in a page that has Space Grotesk
# loaded, so the boxes are sized to the site's font.
config:
  theme: base
  htmlLabels: false
  fontFamily: "'Space Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif"
  flowchart:
    curve: linear
    padding: 16
    nodeSpacing: 24
    rankSpacing: 40
    diagramPadding: 2
  themeVariables:
    darkMode: true
    background: transparent
    fontFamily: "'Space Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif"
    fontSize: 15px
    primaryColor: "#06080c"
    primaryTextColor: "#f2f4f9"
    primaryBorderColor: "#2e3a4e"
    nodeBorder: "#2e3a4e"
    mainBkg: "#06080c"
    lineColor: "#00e5ff"
    textColor: "#c2c9d8"
---
flowchart LR
  accTitle: The judge's role in a session
  accDescr: Analysts file signed takes. The window closes and the takes roll up. The judge reads the frozen takes and explains where they agree and where they part. Where the session sets new weights, it advises updating the target or holding it. The recommendation is published either way, with the advice beside it.
  takes["Analysts file<br/>signed takes"] --> rollup["The window closes<br/>and the takes roll up"]
  rollup --> judge["The judge reads the takes,<br/>where they agree and part"]
  judge --> update["Advice: update<br/>the target"]
  judge --> hold["Advice: hold<br/>the target"]
  update --> publish["Published, with the<br/>advice beside it"]
  hold --> publish
  linkStyle default stroke-width:1.5px
